# sarathi copilot — environment configuration (copy to .env or export)
#
# The service degrades through three tiers depending on which keys exist:
#
#   tier 1 (agentic LLM)  — an LLM key is present AND the model supports
#                           tool/function calling: the model drives the
#                           Toolbox tools itself (multi-turn agent loop).
#   tier 2 (grounded LLM) — an LLM key is present but tool calling fails or
#                           is unsupported: tools are pre-run by keyword
#                           intent and the LLM only phrases the answer from
#                           their JSON output.
#   tier 3 (offline)      — NO LLM key at all: deterministic keyword-intent
#                           templates over live tool data. No LLM anywhere;
#                           every number is grounded by construction. This
#                           is the default and what the test suite runs.
#
# All tiers cite evidence (tool source_ids); if the data backend is also
# unreachable, the service answers honestly that live data is unavailable.

# --- LLM keys (optional — omit both to run tier 3 / offline) ---------------

# Google AI Studio key. If set (and SARATHI_MODEL is not), the service uses
# gemini/gemini-2.5-flash via litellm. Preferred: has a free tier.
#GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OpenAI key. Used only when GEMINI_API_KEY is absent (default gpt-4o-mini).
#OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Explicit litellm model id — overrides the key-based auto-detection above.
# Examples: gemini/gemini-2.5-flash, gpt-4o-mini, anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5.
# The matching provider API key must still be set for litellm to auth.
#SARATHI_MODEL=

# --- Data backend (optional — client-safe defaults are baked in) -----------

# Supabase project URL + anon (publishable) key. The defaults point at the
# YantraFleet demo project; the anon key is the same one the browser console
# embeds, so it is safe to ship.
#SUPABASE_URL=https://flwyvhsmgrrqpmhcqlzd.supabase.co
#SUPABASE_KEY=sb_publishable_7rqvPRggmPDRKNL8Jurcqg_Hf531puf
